# No sample data is committed. Not one byte of it.
#
# This directory is documentation plus a place for fetched samples to land.
# Everything you actually analyse comes from dev-scripts/fetch-samples.sh,
# which pins each file to a size and, where hashed, a SHA-256.
#
# Deny by default, then re-include only the two files that describe the
# arrangement. Written this way round on purpose: a rule listing what to
# exclude fails silently the first time someone adds a format nobody listed,
# which is exactly how data_store/ leaked before it was rewritten the same way
# (defect 7). An allowlist cannot fail that way.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md

# Fetched samples land in large/<group>/. They range from a few KB to 40 GB and
# total 2.8 TB, so they cannot go in git regardless: GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# block applies on every plan, and LFS uploads to lfs.github.com, which some
# networks refuse. Fetch them; never commit them.
large/
